:"அருவி","parts":[{"text":"அருவி","lemma":"அருவி","gloss":"mountain stream"}],"gloss":"mountain streams"},{"surface":"மாறி","parts":[{"text":"மாறு","lemma":"மாறு","gloss":"fail"},{"text":"இ","lemma":"இ","gloss":"having"}],"gloss":"having failed"},{"surface":"அஞ்சுவர","parts":[{"text":"அஞ்சு","lemma":"அஞ்சு","gloss":"fear"},{"text":"வர","lemma":"வர","gloss":"to come"}],"gloss":"frighteningly"},{"surface":"கருகி","parts":[{"text":"கருகு","lemma":"கருகு","gloss":"wither"},{"text":"இ","lemma":"இ","gloss":"having"}],"gloss":"having withered"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"பெருவறம்","parts":[{"text":"பெரு","lemma":"பெரு","gloss":"great"},{"text":"வறம்","lemma":"வறம்","gloss":"drought"}],"gloss":"great drought"},{"surface":"கூர்ந்த","parts":[{"text":"கூர்","lemma":"கூர்","gloss":"abound"},{"text":"ந்","lemma":"ந்","gloss":"nasalization"},{"text":"த்","lemma":"த்","gloss":"past tense marker"},{"text":"அ","lemma":"அ","gloss":"adjectival participle suffix"}],"gloss":"intense"},{"surface":"வேனில்","parts":[{"text":"வேனில்","lemma":"வேனில்","gloss":"summer"}],"gloss":"summer"},{"surface":"காலை","parts":[{"text":"காலை","lemma":"காலை","gloss":"season"}],"gloss":"season"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"பசித்த","parts":[{"text":"பசி","lemma":"பசி","gloss":"hunger"},{"text":"த்","lemma":"த்","gloss":"glide"},{"text":"த்","lemma":"த்","gloss":"past tense marker"},{"text":"அ","lemma":"அ","gloss":"adjectival participle suffix"}],"gloss":"hungry"},{"surface":"ஆயத்து","parts":[{"text":"ஆயத்து","lemma":"ஆயத்து","gloss":"for the herd"}],"gloss":"for the herd","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"பயன்நிரை","parts":[{"text":"பயன்","lemma":"பயன்","gloss":"yield"},{"text":"நிரை","lemma":"நிரை","gloss":"herd"}],"gloss":"yielding herd"},{"surface":"தருமார்","parts":[{"text":"தரு","lemma":"தரு","gloss":"give"},{"text":"மார்","lemma":"மார்","gloss":"in order to"}],"gloss":"in order to feed"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"பூவாள்","parts":[{"text":"பூ","lemma":"பூ","gloss":"flower"},{"text":"வாள்","lemma":"வாள்","gloss":"hook/sickle"}],"gloss":"with flower-hooks"},{"surface":"கோவலர்","parts":[{"text":"கோவலர்","lemma":"கோவலர்","gloss":"herdsmen"}],"gloss":"herdsmen"},{"surface":"பூவுடன்","parts":[{"text":"பூ","lemma":"பூ","gloss":"flower"},{"text":"உடன்","lemma":"உடன்","gloss":"along with"}],"gloss":"along with flowers"},{"surface":"உதிர","parts":[{"text":"உதிர்","lemma":"உதிர்","gloss":"shed"},{"text":"அ","lemma":"அ","gloss":"infinitival suffix"}],"gloss":"to fall"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"கொய்து","parts":[{"text":"கொய்","lemma":"கொய்","gloss":"pluck"},{"text":"து","lemma":"து","gloss":"having"}],"gloss":"plucking"},{"surface":"கட்டு","parts":[{"text":"கட்டு","lemma":"கட்டு","gloss":"branches"}],"gloss":"branches"},{"surface":"அழித்த","parts":[{"text":"அழி","lemma":"அழி","gloss":"destroy"},{"text":"த்","lemma":"த்","gloss":"past tense marker"},{"text":"த்","lemma":"த்","gloss":"glide"},{"text":"அ","lemma":"அ","gloss":"adjectival participle suffix"}],"gloss":"stripped"},{"surface":"வேங்கையின்","parts":[{"text":"வேங்கை","lemma":"வேங்கை","gloss":"Kino tree"},{"text":"இன்","lemma":"இன்","gloss":"like"}],"gloss":"like the Vengai tree"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"மெல்லியல்","parts":[{"text":"மெல்","lemma":"மெல்","gloss":"gentle"},{"text":"இயல்","lemma":"இயல்","gloss":"nature"}],"gloss":"gentle-natured"},{"surface":"மகளிரும்","parts":[{"text":"மகளிர்","lemma":"மகளிர்","gloss":"wives"},{"text":"உம்","lemma":"உம்","gloss":"too"}],"gloss":"wives too"},{"surface":"இழை","parts":[{"text":"இழை","lemma":"இழை","gloss":"ornaments"}],"gloss":"their ornaments"},{"surface":"களைந்தனரே","parts":[{"text":"களை","lemma":"களை","gloss":"remove"},{"text":"ந்","lemma":"ந்","gloss":"nasalization"},{"text":"த்","lemma":"த்","gloss":"past tense marker"},{"text":"அனர்","lemma":"அனர்","gloss":"they"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ஏ","gloss":"indeed"}],"gloss":"have discarded indeed"}]}],"literal":"Without regarding fortresses, conquering in battles / with companions, emptying jars of liquor / cherishing the large families of bards / in the court of glorious justice where righteousness is fully examined / praised by those who know justice well standing in front / with wives of pure nature and blemishless vows / within the fortress walls of sun-like shape and many defenses / where vultures eat at the tall sacrificial posts / completing the Vedic sacrificial rites / he indeed knew, the wise king / he passed away; pitiable is this world! / Mountain streams failing, frighteningly withered / in the summer season of intense great drought / to feed the hungry herd of yielding cattle / herdsmen with flower-hooks, so that flowers fall / like the Vengai tree stripped of its plucked branches / the gentle-natured wives too have discarded their ornaments.","translation":"He who conquered battles without caring for fortresses, who emptied jars of liquor with his close companions, who sustained the large families of great bards, who was praised by wise men standing before him in the court of glorious justice where righteousness was fully examined, who, along with his wives of pure nature and blemishless vows, completed Vedic sacrificial rites at the tall sacrificial posts where vultures feed, within the sun-shaped fortress walls of many defenses— that wise king indeed knew how to live. But now he has passed away! How pitiable is this world! Just like the Vengai tree in the harsh summer of intense drought, when mountain streams fail and everything is frighteningly withered, is stripped of its branches by herdsmen using flower-hooks to make the leaves and flowers fall to feed their hungry cattle, his gentle-natured wives have now discarded all their ornaments.","modern":"கோட்டைகளைக் கருதாமல் போர்களை வென்றதும், தன் தோழர்களோடு சேர்ந்து மதுக்குடங்களை வெறுமையாக்கியதும், பாணர்களின் பெரிய சுற்றத்தாரைக் காப்பாற்றியதும், அறம் தவறாமல் ஆராயும் பெருமைமிக்க அவையத்தில் நீதியை நன்கு அறிந்தவர்கள் முன்னின்று புகழும்படி வாழ்ந்ததும், தூய்மையான இயல்பும் குற்றமற்ற விரதமும் உடைய தன் மனைவியரோடு கூடி, சூரியனைப் போன்ற வட்ட வடிவமான மதில்களைக் கொண்ட கோட்டையினுள், கழுகுகள் பலி உணவை உண்ணும் யூப நெடுந்தூண்களை நட்டு வேத வேள்விகளைச் செய்து முடித்ததும் ஆகிய அனைத்தையும் அந்த அறிவுடைய அரசன் நன்கு அறிந்திருந்தான். ஆனால், அவன் இப்போது இறந்துவிட்டான். இந்த உலகம் மிகவும் இரங்கத்தக்கது! அருவிகள் வற்றி, அஞ்சத்தக்க வகையில் கருகிப் பெரும் வறட்சி மிகுந்த கோடைகாலத்தில், பசியோடு இருக்கும் தன் பசுக்கூட்டங்களுக்கு உணவளிக்க விரும்பிய இடையர்கள், பூக்கள் உதிரும்படி வளைந்த கவராற் கொய்து கிளைகளை ஒடித்த வேங்கை மரத்தைப் போல, மென்மையான இயல்புடைய அவனுடைய மனைவியரும் தங்கள் அணிகலன்களைக் களைந்துவிட்டனர்.","explanation":"This poem belongs to the Potuviyal tiṇai and Kaiyaṟunilai tuṟai, composed by Karuṅkuḻal Ātaṉār on the death of the great Chola king Karikāṟ Peruvaḷattāṉ. The poet laments the loss of the king, praising his valor in battle, his generosity to bards, his adherence to justice in court, and his performance of Vedic sacrifices alongside his virtuous wives. The central image of the poem is a powerful simile comparing the widowed queens to a Vengai tree in summer. Just as herdsmen strip the Vengai tree of its leafy branches to feed their starving cattle during a severe drought, leaving the tree bare, the gentle queens have stripped themselves of all their beautiful ornaments in their grief. This poignant comparison highlights the devastating impact of the king's death on his household and his kingdom, transforming a once-glorious court into a place of desolation.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"}}